WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.012
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:09.559
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:16.912
Unit ten: Cultural Diplomacy. Today you will use verbs that change meaning with -ing or to-infinitive.

4
00:00:17.212 --> 00:00:19.748
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.037
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.047
Soft power.

7
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:32.080
Soft power means the ability to win support through attraction rather than force.

8
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.229
Music and film give a country soft power.

9
00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:39.247
Your turn. Say: Soft power.

10
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.322
Soft power.

11
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.932
Cultural exchange program.

12
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:52.097
Cultural exchange program means a scheme that sends students or artists to live and learn abroad.

13
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:55.855
A cultural exchange program sent dancers to Japan.

14
00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.008
Your turn. Say: Cultural exchange program.

15
00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:05.191
Cultural exchange program.

16
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.439
Public diplomacy.

17
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:13.433
Public diplomacy means a government's efforts to explain its views to foreign citizens.

18
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:17.537
Public diplomacy includes interviews and festivals.

19
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.267
Your turn. Say: Public diplomacy.

20
00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.622
Public diplomacy.

21
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:27.744
National image.

22
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.851
National image means the picture of a country that people around the world hold.

23
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.728
Tourism improved the national image.

24
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:39.224
Your turn. Say: National image.

25
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.660
National image.

26
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.731
Cultural export.

27
00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:51.572
Cultural export means a film, song or tradition that a country shares with the world.

28
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:55.355
Traditional dance became a popular cultural export.

29
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.893
Your turn. Say: Cultural export.

30
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.280
Cultural export.

31
00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:05.807
People-to-people ties.

32
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:11.730
People-to-people ties means friendly links between ordinary citizens of different countries.

33
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:15.489
People-to-people ties survive political disagreements.

34
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:19.769
Your turn. Say: People-to-people ties.

35
00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:24.412
People-to-people ties.

36
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.627
International goodwill.

37
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:31.462
International goodwill means friendly feelings between nations.

38
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.572
The concert created international goodwill.

39
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:38.161
Your turn. Say: International goodwill.

40
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.907
International goodwill.

41
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.023
Cultural influence.

42
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:51.081
Cultural influence means the ability of a culture to shape the tastes of other societies.

43
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:54.693
Korean television has great cultural influence.

44
00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:58.644
Your turn. Say: Cultural influence.

45
00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.058
Cultural influence.

46
00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:07.448
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:08.283 --> 00:03:14.593
Visal, a diplomat says 'I remember attending the festival' and 'Remember to attend the festival'. Why are the forms different?

48
00:03:15.683 --> 00:03:30.787
Some verbs change meaning. Remember + -ing is a memory of a past event. Remember + to-infinitive is a duty not to forget. Forget, regret, stop and try work the same way.

49
00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:33.616
Can you show more examples?

50
00:03:34.717 --> 00:03:46.079
'The ministry regrets to announce a delay' is news now. 'The ministry regrets announcing the ban' is sorrow about the past. 'She stopped to watch' differs from 'She stopped watching'.

51
00:03:47.183 --> 00:03:49.055
Why does it matter in diplomacy?

52
00:03:50.150 --> 00:04:01.350
Precision avoids misunderstanding. 'Try offering exchange programmes' suggests an experiment, while 'try to offer' means make an effort. Diplomats choose their words carefully.

53
00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.047
Part three: grammar.

54
00:04:04.883 --> 00:04:09.704
Grammar focus: Verb plus -ing or to-infinitive (meaning changes).

55
00:04:10.004 --> 00:04:11.249
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.470
The envoy remembers attending the first cultural exchange program.

57
00:04:16.383 --> 00:04:19.358
The ministry regrets to announce that the tour is cancelled.

58
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.364
Officials tried offering free concerts to win goodwill.

59
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:33.010
Remember / forget / regret / stop / try change meaning: + -ing looks back or experiments; + to-infinitive is a duty, a purpose or current news.

60
00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.935
Be careful! Don't say: I remember to visit it as a child.

61
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.329
Say: I remember visiting it as a child.

62
00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:45.337
Use remember + -ing for a past memory.

63
00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.530
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:50.892
The Power of Culture.

65
00:04:51.192 --> 00:04:55.397
Soft power means winning friends through attraction rather than force.

66
00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.523
Many people remember watching a film or hearing a song that changed how they saw another country.

67
00:05:02.533 --> 00:05:09.096
A cultural export such as music or cuisine improves a national image, and public diplomacy tries to build on it.

68
00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:16.732
A cultural exchange program lets students live abroad, and people-to-people ties create lasting international goodwill.

69
00:05:17.733 --> 00:05:23.634
Governments should not forget to support artists, because their cultural influence travels farther than speeches.

70
00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:28.990
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.931
Don't forget blank the visa form.

72
00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.536
A, signing. B, to sign. C, sign.

73
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.227
The answer is B: to sign.

74
00:05:42.383 --> 00:05:44.894
I remember blank the exhibition last year.

75
00:05:45.194 --> 00:05:48.719
A, to visit. B, visiting. C, visit.

76
00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.382
The answer is B: visiting.

77
00:05:55.517 --> 00:05:59.850
Sharing a country's music, films and food abroad is a cultural blank.

78
00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.780
A, export. B, dispute. C, debris.

79
00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.228
The answer is A: export.

80
00:06:10.383 --> 00:06:12.220
Which sentence gives news now?

81
00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:19.866
A, We regret to inform you of the delay.. B, We regret informing you of the delay.. C, We regret inform you of the delay..

82
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.851
The answer is A: We regret to inform you of the delay..

83
00:06:28.017 --> 00:06:30.968
According to the reading, soft power wins friends through…

84
00:06:31.268 --> 00:06:34.550
A, force. B, attraction. C, tariffs.

85
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.483
The answer is B: attraction.

86
00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.516
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:49.869
Can you think of an example of cultural diplomacy, like music, film, or sports?

88
00:06:58.683 --> 00:07:00.021
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:00.321 --> 00:07:24.431
One example is a national football team playing a friendly match in another country. Fans celebrate together, players meet ordinary people and the visit improves the national image of both sides. Concerts, films and food festivals work in the same way: they build goodwill and soft power without the pressure of political negotiation.

90
00:07:24.731 --> 00:07:26.371
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:27.283 --> 00:07:33.268
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb plus -ing or to-infinitive (meaning changes).

92
00:07:33.568 --> 00:07:39.320
Today's value is cultural appreciation. Enjoy and respect the music and art of every culture.

93
00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.563
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

94
00:07:42.863 --> 00:07:45.712
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

